Dead-token rings — strongest idea. Keep failed tokens permanently. Walking past hundreds of stands showing -99.98%, HOLDERS: 2, LAST TRADE: 391 DAYS AGO, LIQUIDITY: $4.21 makes the market's history physical. No invented horror content is necessary.
Players as distant silhouettes — don't show usernames at range. In the darkness you just see somebody standing at a terminal or crossing a pool of light. Voice and footsteps can reveal that someone is nearby before you see them.
Terminal proximity wake-up — dead stands stay almost completely black until you approach. At ~2–3 m the monitor quietly powers on and reveals the token's actual history. When you walk away, it slowly goes dark again. This also helps performance.
